decisions:
  - id: ship-crew-skip-if-exists
    decision: Ship Mika (designer), Lux, Quill, Iris .agent files in the studio templates, skip-if-exists
    rationale: They lived only in the owner's ~/.paradigm, so other machines got Luna without Mika's vetting rules; skip-if-exists never clobbers a user's own or learned copy.
  - id: record-cli-path
    decision: setup records `cli:` (atelier or node <path>) in ~/.atelier/config.yaml and skills use it
    rationale: A source build doesn't put atelier on PATH; recording the path makes episode runs work without forcing a global npm link.
  - id: devengines-guard
    decision: devEngines packageManager=pnpm onFail=error plus a preinstall check
    rationale: npm resolves deps before preinstall, so preinstall alone never fires on npm 11; devEngines fails fast with a clear message.
  - id: in-repo-install-skill
    decision: Project-level .claude/skills/atelier-install in the repo
    rationale: Claude in a fresh clone otherwise has no idea how to get atelier design working; the skill defers to atelier-design once installed.
errors_encountered:
  - description: '`git commit -qam` committed .paradigm session/event files and .claude/settings.local.json'
    resolution: Soft reset before pushing; recommitted only setup.ts
    time_to_fix: 1 min
learnings:
  - Earlier advice to a user (`npm install` in the clone) was wrong — always smoke-test install instructions on a fresh clone with an empty HOME/PATH before giving them.
  - '`git commit -a` in this repo sweeps in Paradigm session/event files and settings.local.json; stage paths explicitly.'
verification:
